  <li><a href="#hx-3"><b>03</b>Editorial, oversized</a></li>
  <li><a href="#hx-4"><b>04</b>Wordmark ground</a></li>
  <li><a href="#hx-5"><b>05</b>Three doors</a></li>
</ul>

<!-- 01 -->
<section class="hx-option" id="hx-1">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hx-cap"><p>01 · Recommended</p><p><b>Centred statement</b>One idea, dead centre: a release pill, the headline at full size, one sentence and one clear action, with a quiet link beside it. The three products step back to a single hairline row at the foot, so the screen has one thing to say.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="hx-stage hx-1">
    <span class="hx-glow"></span>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hx-1-body hx-in">
        <a class="hx-pill" href="https://github.com/Sage-is/AI-UI" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i>New</i>Sage AI-UI v3.2.0 is out</a>
        <h2 class="hx-title">Your next <span class="text-accent">AI breakthrough</span></h2>
        <p class="hx-lede">Decades of experience building AI before ChatGPT. We create custom solutions and open-source tools to grow your business.</p>
        <div class="hx-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="https://sage.is/programs#packages">Start a project {{ arrow | safe }}</a>
          <a class="hx-link" href="https://github.com/Sage-is/AI-UI" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ github | safe }} Star on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hx-1-foot">
        <span>Makers of</span>
        {% for p in products %}<a href="{{ p.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ p.name }}</a>{% endfor %}
        <span>· Hundreds of students already build with Sage</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 -->
<section class="hx-option" id="hx-2">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hx-cap"><p>02 · Show it</p><p><b>Split, with the product</b>Copy on the left, the product on the right: a calm Sage AI-UI window where a question is asked and answered as the hero comes into view. It shows what Sage does before anyone reads a word, and carries the intro's prompt into the page.</p></div>
